  "created": "2026-10-25T20:53:25.517Z",
  "description": "EvoPdf Next Excel to PDF Converter for .NET (Linux ARM64) is a component of the EvoPdf Next Library for .NET that enables accurate conversion of complex Excel documents to PDF.\n\nThe converter targets .NET Standard 2.0 and can be used in .NET Core and .NET Framework applications deployed on Windows, Linux and macOS, including Azure, AWS, Google Cloud, Docker and Kubernetes.\n\nThis package installs only the Linux ARM64 runtime. For Linux x64, the additional package EvoPdf.Next.ExcelToPdf.Linux can be referenced on its own or alongside this package.\n\nSeparate packages are available for Windows, macOS or multi-platform runtimes.\n\nCompatibility:\n\n* Linux (ARM64) - Debian 11+, Ubuntu 20.04+ or equivalent\n* .NET 10.0, 9.0, 8.0, 7.0, 6.0 and .NET Standard 2.0\n* AWS Elastic Beanstalk and AWS Lambda on Graviton\n* Linux Virtual Machines\n* Docker containers and Kubernetes for Linux\n* Web, Console and Desktop applications\n\nMain Features:\n\n* Convert Excel XLSX documents from memory or from a file to PDF\n* Use the PDF page settings from the original Excel document\n* Use the page settings from the first or the active worksheet\n* Use custom PDF page settings to automatically reflow the content\n* Convert all worksheets or only the first worksheet\n* Display or hide the worksheet title\n* Keep the column widths and row heights from Excel\n* Add HTML headers, footers or stamps to the generated PDF\n* Control the PDF document display with PDF viewer preferences\n* Encrypt, set permissions and set passwords for the generated PDF documents\n* Add digital signatures to the generated PDF document\n* Asynchronous methods for async and await\n\nDocumentation and code samples:\nhttps://www.evopdf.com/evopdf-next-excel-xlsx-to-pdf-dotnet",
